In a video statement, Praveen Goyal said the allegation that his daughter showed a middle finger to the media was false.

“Siya is being accused of showing the middle finger. It is nothing of that sort. When she had come home with the police for legal formalities, two of her fingers got smashed in a car door, which is why there is a bandage on one finger while the other is swollen. Even her nails have turned blue,” he said.

The clarification came after the video went viral on social media, drawing sharp reactions from users online.
Meanwhile, Pune Rural Police has moved a court seeking permission to conduct polygraph tests on Goyal and her alleged associate Chaudhary, an official said.

Officials also said that clothes allegedly worn by Goyal on June 18, the day of the incident, were recovered during a search of her residence in Pune’s Market Yard area.

Goyal (20) and Chaudhary (22) are accused of pushing 25-year-old Agarwal to his death from a cliff at Lohagad Fort in Pune district on June 18. Agarwal and Goyal were scheduled to marry in November.

Following the alleged murder, both Goyal and Chaudhary were arrested and remanded in police custody till July 3.

(With agency inputs)
